Day 34: Mercy Over Judgment | Monday of the Fifth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“Neither do I condemn you.”
Not hesitation.
Not conditions.
Just mercy.

Welcome to Day 34 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection draws you into the tender, restorative heart of Jesus — a heart that meets you not with condemnation, but with compassion. His mercy restores dignity, lifts shame, and opens the door to new beginnings.

This spoken‑word devotional invites you to receive that mercy deeply and to extend it — to yourself, to others, and to the world. Mercy is not weakness; it is strength. The strength to forgive, to let go, and to see others as God sees them.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Jesus meets you with mercy, not condemnation

How mercy restores what shame tries to destroy

Why Lent invites you to receive mercy and offer it freely

A prayer for a softened, merciful heart

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, let mercy lead me.”

